# Collision shapes
@scenario tutorial_lesson_26
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide thoughtful]
ginger: Imagine bumping into an invisible edge. Where something looks solid and where it stops you can be two different shapes.
ginger: In the JES editor, use the example panel as a reference. Compare its drawn bounds with the collision shape you would give it.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What determines whether two physical objects can collide?
> Their displayed colors. -> retry
> Their physics bodies and collision shapes. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: Visual bounds and collision shapes serve different purposes. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: Visual bounds and collision shapes serve different purposes.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_26]
[flag tutorial_done_26]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_5]
